# L §6.4 from D: "A move the scenario declares books nothing before D: an instance whose day, a window's first day, or
# a leg's own day falls before D is left out". extra is dated window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10), which starts before from
# 2027-01-01: left out by its window's first day, whatever day it takes (writer 8: no windows clause is needed;
# windows earliest and latest are gone); late_ is dated 2027-01-05, but its leg's own
# day is 2026-12-28: left out. So konto keeps its opening, 100.00 PLN, in early as in the base. (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §6.4, a scenario move booking before from through a window day or a leg's own day.)
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version base
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask b: bal(konto, 2027-12-31)
=== early.tally
scenario early over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

input xday: date
input lday: date
input legday: date
input xamt: money PLN

move extra: transfers
  on xday
  leg cash from konto to world amount xamt

move late_: transfers
  on lday
  leg cash from konto to world amount xamt on legday

version ex
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-06-01
  xday = window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) "plan"
  xamt = 10.00 PLN "plan"
  lday = 2027-01-05 "plan"
  legday = 2026-12-28 "plan"

ask e: bal(konto, 2027-12-31) in early
=== expect
b: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
e: 100.00 PLN
  world: early
  left out: extra, 1 instances, first 2026-12-20
  left out: late_, 1 instances, first 2027-01-05
  cut 2026-10-20
